      "verdict": "met",
      "justification": "The candidate correctly identifies that the statutory threshold is more than 20 employees under art. 74, § 2º, da CLT, and that a company with 15 employees is not obliged to keep time records."
    },
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "verdict": "met",
      "justification": "The candidate explicitly concludes that the non-presentation of time records does not generate a presumption of truthfulness of the alleged working hours (Súmula 338 presumption does not apply)."
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "verdict": "met",
      "justification": "The candidate notes that the statutory wording prevails over the outdated numerical parameter of Súmula 338, I, of the TST, resolving the conflict in favor of the statute."
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "verdict": "met",
      "justification": "The candidate correctly places the burden of proof on the claimant (Pedro) as a constitutive fact of his right, citing art. 818, I, of the CLT."
    }
  ],
  "verdict": "correct",
  "contradicts_gold": false
}
